@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:architecture;concurrency] no-transaction-across-temporal
No FDB transaction MAY stay open across a Temporal RPC. FDB reads, FDB writes, and Temporal client
calls MUST run in activities, never in workflow code.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:backend;error-handling] dirty-keys-are-the-work
Pending work MUST be recorded only in FDB outbox events and dirty keys. Losing a `wake` signal, a
workflow, or a worker MUST NOT lose work: the relay MUST find it again from FDB.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:architecture] payload-free-wake
`wake` signals MUST carry no payload. Stage workflows MUST read their work from FDB.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:architecture] index-stage-owns-elasticsearch
Only the index stage MAY write to Elasticsearch.

@cc [owner:flvndvd,label:performance] bounded-workflow-history
Workflow inputs, results, and state MUST hold only stage identifiers, tenant IDs, object IDs,
cursors, counts, and timestamps, never file bytes or extracted text.
